<!-- CONVERTED — VISUALLY VERIFIED --><chapter xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude" xml:id="ch06-shape-extremes-and-the-mean-value-theorem">
  <title>Shape, Extremes, and the Mean Value Theorem</title>
  <shorttitle>Shape and the Mean Value Theorem</shorttitle>

  <introduction><p>Derivatives describe more than rates of change. Their signs determine intervals of increase and decrease, and second derivatives describe concavity. This chapter connects derivative information to extrema and graph shape, proves Rolle's Theorem and the Mean Value Theorem, and applies these results to limits and estimates.</p></introduction>

